# docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore — what the build context carries into the image.
#
# BuildKit honours this file for builds of `docker/Dockerfile` (verified on Docker 29.8.1 with
# `-f <dir>/Dockerfile.<name>` and a `<dir>/Dockerfile.<name>.dockerignore` companion, 2026-09-27),
# which is why this repository needs no root-level `.dockerignore`: the rule lives next to the
# Dockerfile it belongs to, inside the lane that owns it.
#
# WHAT THIS PREVENTS, beyond a slow build: without it the image would carry the HOST's node_modules,
# .git, evidence and toolchain scratch, and the container's `bun install` could then "succeed" on
# modules the host happened to have — a fake green. The entrypoint asserts the filtering held
# (`copy.contextFiltered`) rather than trusting this file silently.
#
# Patterns are relative to the CONTEXT ROOT (the repository root). `dist` therefore matches the
# repository's packed output at the root ONLY; `packages/*/dist` is deliberately kept, because the
# container rebuilds every one of those entries from source and that rebuild is an assertion.

# version-control history: an install must not need it
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# dependencies: `bun install` recreates them inside the container
node_modules
**/node_modules

# this repository's packed distribution (a source-tree test never consumes it)
dist

# host-local QA and toolchain state
evidence
.qa-*
.toolchain
.codegraph
.t18ev
.t28ev
.bun-tmp
.mpd

# this case's own scratch
docker/out
docker/.selftest
